headers {
  x-api-key: {{process.env.API_KEY}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

docs {
  Auth is declared once here, at collection level. Copying the header into every
  request would drift the moment the header name changes.

  The key itself is never committed: it comes from a gitignored bruno/.env,
  which Bruno auto-loads as process.env. See bruno/.env.example.

  Every request that writes creates records named with the BRUNO_TEST_ prefix
  and deletes them again at the end of its chain. The collection points at
  whatever baseUrl says, and during development that is the real database
  holding real personal finances — the marker is what makes debris from an
  aborted run identifiable. The Cleanup folder removes anything left behind.
}
